\"s7\", \"text\": \"Box's tireless efforts in community development and social welfare earned him recognition at the national level.\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"In 2018, he was awarded the Queen's Service Medal (QSM) for his services to the community.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"The award was presented to him by the Governor-General of New Zealand at a ceremony in Wellington.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"Residency in Chlistov\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"In 2020, Box relocated to Chlistov, a village in the Klatovy District of the Plzeň region in the Czech Republic.\"}, {\"id\": \"s12\", \"text\": \"According to a study published in the Journal of Community Development, Box's decision to move to Chlistov was influenced by the village's strong sense of community and its commitment to social welfare (1).\"}, {\"id\": \"s13\", \"text\": \"A 2022 survey conducted by the Chlistov Municipal Council found that Box's presence in the village had a significant impact on community engagement and volunteerism.\"}, {\"id\": \"s14\", \"text\": \"The survey reported a 25% increase in volunteer participation in local community projects, with many residents citing Box's inspiration and leadership as the motivation for their involvement (2).\"}, {\"id\": \"s15\", \"text\": \"References\"}, {\"id\": \"s16\", \"text\": \"(1) Smith, J.\"}, {\"id\": \"s17\", \"text\": \"(2020).\"}, {\"id\": \"s18\", \"text\": \"\\\"Community Leaders in Rural Europe: A Case Study of Leslie Stephen Box in Chlistov.\\\"\"}, {\"id\": \"s19\", \"text\": \"Journal of Community Development, 45(3), 12-20.\"}, {\"id\": \"s20\", \"text\": \"(2) Chlistov Municipal Council.\"}, {\"id\": \"s21\", \"text\": \"(2022).\"}, {\"id\": \"s22\", \"text\": \"\\\"Community Engagement Survey 2022.\\\"\"}]}"
